schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: "The Promise: Coordination, Transparency, and New Economic Models"
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: concept
  summary: >-
    A high-level orientation to why web3 excites regens beyond money: DAOs,
    quadratic voting, and futarchy as coordination-without-central-control
    tools; blockchain transparency as verifiable (not "transparency theater")
    accountability; and new economic models (credentialing via POAPs/Gitcoin/
    retroactive funding, community value capture, and impact-aligned
    instruments like regenerative tokens and outcome-based bonds).
  audience: regens evaluating whether web3 coordination tools are worth exploring
  known_tensions:
    - experimental-and-imperfect-tools vs genuinely-new-coordination-possibilities
  related_concepts:
    - dao
    - quadratic-voting
    - futarchy
    - retroactive-public-goods-funding
  related_resources:
    - Snapshot
    - Radicle
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/coordination-transparency.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-97dd78ba716a
  source_lineage: coordination-transparency.md
  notes: |
    # assessed-but-excluded
    - article is thin on citations (mostly definitional/promotional claims about
      web3 capabilities with no sourcing); treated as concept overview rather
      than claim-evidence since there is no specific verifiable figure to
      isolate as a claim.
